## E10b the docs warning: a user with ~tenant1:* +@all can still FLUSHALL; -flushall removes it
$ redis-cli -p 7206 ACL SETUSER tenant1 on >test-only-2 ~tenant1:* +@all
OK
$ redis-cli -p 7206 SET other:keep 1
OK
AUTH tenant1 -> +OK
GET other:keep -> -NOPERM No permissions to access a key
FLUSHALL (user has ~tenant1:* +@all) -> +OK
$ redis-cli -p 7206 DBSIZE
0
$ redis-cli -p 7206 ACL DELUSER cacheapp tenant1
2

## E11 maxclients: the 6th connection is refused with an error and counted in rejected_connections
$ redis-cli -p 7206 CONFIG SET maxclients 5
OK
connection 1 -> b'+PONG'
connection 2 -> b'+PONG'
connection 3 -> b'+PONG'
connection 4 -> b'+PONG'
connection 5 -> b'+PONG'
connection 6 -> b'-ERR max number of clients reached'
connection 7 -> b'-ERR max number of clients reached'
connection 8 -> b'-ERR max number of clients reached'
$ redis-cli -p 7206 INFO | grep -E 'rejected_connections|connected_clients'
connected_clients:1
rejected_connections:3

## (redis-cli itself holds one slot while measuring, hence only 4 of the probe connections succeeded after it)
$ redis-cli -p 7206 CONFIG SET maxclients 10000
OK

## E12 client eviction (maxmemory-clients, Redis 7.0+): a slow reader that never reads its replies
$ redis-cli -p 7206 SET bigv 
OK
$ redis-cli -p 7206 CONFIG SET maxmemory-clients 20mb
OK
sent 400 requests without reading any reply
$ redis-cli -p 7206 INFO stats | grep -E 'evicted_clients|client_output_buffer_limit_disconnections'
evicted_clients:0
client_output_buffer_limit_disconnections:0
$ redis-cli -p 7206 INFO | grep -E 'connected_clients|mem_clients_normal'
connected_clients:1
mem_clients_normal:0
mem_clients_normal_shared:0
mem_clients_normal_unshared:0
$ redis-cli -p 7206 CONFIG SET maxmemory-clients 0
OK
$ redis-cli -p 7206 DEL bigv
1
